0..74 Comment "// An `extern \"rust\"` block outside the form or its row, and an undeclared"
75..113 Comment "// call, each refused where it stands."
114..116 Comment "//"
117..194 Comment "// A member\'s types are the four fixed-width atoms, which cross as the values"
195..274 Comment "// the runtime holds. A wider type needs a layout to cross by, and the lowering"
275..353 Comment "// reads none yet. A block naming its members\' rows is admitted only when each"
354..413 Comment "// declared type has its row\'s layout under Rust\'s default."
414..416 Comment "//"
417..496 Comment "// The first block\'s member takes an `Integer` and is refused at that type. The"
497..572 Comment "// second declares its count `u64` against a row of two `u32`, so its check"
573..643 Comment "// fails on size. The third declares only `add`, so `less` performs an"
644..677 Comment "// operation it does not declare."
678..680 Comment "//"
681..745 Comment "// - owes: #327 — a member\'s type beyond the fixed-width atoms"
746..823 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr` — the form, called from"
824..863 Comment "//   Rust, and admitted against its row"
865..939 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
